        {
          "id": 3498776141,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "> Doing this (which is what the gzip handling code does) seems to result in a LZ4 frame header wrapped around zero data instead of an empty file.\n\nI.e., it results in one of those rare cases where \"compression\" increases the size of the file. :-)\n\n`unlz4` appears to read an empty file and \"uncompressed\" it to an empty file, so the empty file *could* be considered an empty file.\n\n`gunzip`, not so much:\n\n```\n$ gunzip empty.gz\ngunzip: empty.gz: unexpected end of file\n```\n\nso *maybe* that's a case for gzip writing out a gzip header even if no data has been written.\n\nAnd perhaps there are other lz4 uncompressers that don't handle empty files the way `unlz4` does, so maybe we *should* write out a header... and indicate, in both the gzip and lz4 code, why we're doing that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-06-26T19:51:30.627Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-26T19:51:32.030Z",
          "system": false,
