        {
          "id": 3500295497,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "What *Wireshark* does, since we look at the file contents not the extension (it's the UN*X way), is end up treating the empty file as an uncompressed file, and then usually one of the libwiretap heuristic file formats will accept it as a degenerate zero frame case - right now it seems that the ERF reader does that first, but that could change depending on ordering.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
